{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/126252-projects-of-the-god-machine","id":126252,"title":"Projects (of the God-Machine)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-05T16:48:31-07:00","id":126252,"title":"Projects (of the God-Machine)","content":"Any ideas what the God-Machine might want accomplished, and how It might go about it? Come up with any great example Projects or Infrastructure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","name":"William Louison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T10:54:14-07:00","id":126801,"title":"","content":"Okay, I guess I'll try and get the ball rolling, so here's <b>Project: Fat Man</b><br /> <br /> A Divine Subroutine of the God-Machine decided it wanted to gather more information on human ethical reasoning. While crunching a vast array of moral philosophy literature, it came upon a suitable structure for a field experiment. If you've ever taken a philosophy course, you're probably familiar with the ethical thought experiment known as The Trolley Problem (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolley_problem\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trolley_problem</a>), which tests the ethical choices of human beings in various circumstances. This facet of the GM decides to set up the infrastructure necessary to conduct the experiments in the field, on live humans, so it can come up with a statistical database that will predict human decision-making in life-or-death situations.<br /> <br /> The necessary infrastructure would be quite extensive: human or angelic agents would have to acquire multiple train yards and trains, specially modifying each to make the terms of the thought experiment possible (each train would have to be modified so that it could be easily derailed by impacting a fat man). They would need a large supply human captives (especially fat men) to tie to the tracks. And they would need Concealment infrastructure to disguise these events from mortals.<br /> <br /> I feel proud that I've devised a scenario which could potentially involve World of Darkness PCs rescuing a damsel tied to railroad tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","user":"William Louison","date":". 05-06-2014, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","name":"William Louison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T17:44:49-07:00","id":127864,"title":"","content":"Project: Watchman. This was the central plot of our crossover game. The infrastructure needed was quite unique. The Linchpin was an Arisen, who (over the course of several decades) was &quot;reprogrammed&quot; into service of the Machine. Angels worked to build a suitable tomb for it, one that glorified the God-Machine (who the mummy called Atun). One angel was designed to be his &quot;wife&quot;, serving as an anchor for his artificial history. She had a rough start (a few models of the wife were utterly destroyed before the repeated deathcycles washed away his past), but by the time the game started, the mummy was convinced he had loved her forever, and had a divine duty to serve Atun and his divine will. The project required extensive infrastructure, including a way to contain the mummy in case of memory returning, an HK terminator angel designed specifically to put down the Mummy if necessary, various Relics and iremite ritual knowledge and tools, and the corpse of the mummy's wife (linchpin of the angelic &quot;wife&quot;). The output of the project--a near endlessly reusable agent that could be activated for tasks that require a very heavy, night indestructable hand. Some jobs would be wasteful to send angels to accomplish, as the likelyhood of destruction is too high. So.. the Machine activates the Wife, who then activates the Mummy, giving it a Purpose designed by holy Atun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T19:37:20-07:00","id":127932,"title":"","content":"In regards to watchman, don't mummies need their connection for power(haven't read but heard about)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T10:15:38-07:00","id":128346,"title":"","content":"It had a functional tomb. Wasn't great to mummy standards, but it was enough to sleep well and regenerate its power. He still goes through the regular death cycles of a Mummy, rising with great power to accomplish the purposes of his cult (ie his wife and her mortal pawns). Through trial, error, and patience, the wife &quot;trained&quot; the Memory out of it through a few deaths and several very, very bad Purposes to whittle away his humanity. Of course, the plan eventually fails spectacularly in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}